 "notes": "Observed 95% CL limit from Fig. 7 (left), photon-only coupling scenario (operator a F Ftilde / 4Lambda; g_agamma = 1/Lambda in GeV^-1, matching the canonical convention up to an irrelevant sign). Curve extracted from the vector paths of Figure_007-a.pdf in the arXiv e-print; axis calibration from tick-mark coordinates (linear mass axis 10-100 GeV, log coupling axis with decades at 1e-4 and 1e-3). Vertices of the drawn curve are at m_a ~ 5, 6, 9, 11, 14, 16, 22, 30, 90, 100 GeV; intermediate points are log-linear interpolation along the drawn straight segments. Paper quotes the limit range as m_a = 5-90 GeV; the plotted curve extends to the frame edge at 100 GeV. The alternative hypercharge-coupling scenario (Fig. 7 right) is not reported. Collider limit: no dark-matter density assumption.",
